    slug: 'riverside', name: 'Riverside', tone: 'mint', category: 'Recording studio with AI editing',
    hook: 'Record anywhere. Edit on your own computer.',
    description: 'AgentShot vs Riverside: a free, open-source Riverside alternative for editing recordings locally with your own AI model, no watermark and no upload.',
    verdict: 'AgentShot is the better choice for the edit. Riverside is a recording studio first, with an online editor attached; AgentShot is the editor, on your own computer, with the model you choose, free and never watermarked. It cuts the filler, keeps the right speaker in frame, makes the Shorts and shows every change as a before/after version, then goes further than a podcast tool: motion graphics, product demos filmed from a URL, and timelines for Premiere, Resolve or Final Cut.',
    overview: 'Riverside records remote interviews and podcasts, capturing each participant locally in up to 4K on separate tracks, and live streams to several destinations. Around that it has built an online editor: transcript editing, Magic Clips, filler-word and silence removal, and Co-Creator, a chat agent in the editor’s sidebar. To use any of it, your content is recorded on or uploaded to Riverside, with Riverside’s AI; the reviewed pages do not name the model. The reviewed Free plan lists up to 720p video and a Riverside watermark, with watermark-free 4K on paid plans and AI credits for features such as translation and B-roll. Bring-your-own model keys, editing without uploading and filming a product from a URL are not documented on the reviewed pages.',
